Summit Software finished the quarter with $1.5M in cash and reported revenue of $1.8M for the quarter (annualized ~$7.2M). Our current reported cash burn is $45K/month, which—if that is the net cash outflow—translates into roughly 33 months of runway. This positions us with substantial flexibility to invest in prioritized growth initiatives while maintaining conservative contingency. If the board approves near-term hiring/product investments that raise the monthly net burn to an estimated $75K, runway would reduce to ~20 months and we recommend setting fundraising or cash-preservation milestones accordingly. Key focus areas: maintain ARR momentum, accelerate collections on large enterprise deals, and finalize a fundraising contingency plan aligned to hiring/investment milestones.

