"Summit Software finished the quarter with $1.5M in cash and $1.8M in revenue last quarter (annualized run-rate ~$7.2M). Our reported runway is 20 months, which implies a net burn nearer $75K/month when considering upcoming hiring and planned investments. While current revenue provides strong top-line momentum, planned investments in sales and product expansion have increased monthly cash requirements.

We recommend a two-track approach: (1) accelerate revenue conversion and tighten spend where ROI is poor; (2) prepare a targeted raise to preserve flexibility and avoid a forced timetable. We should present fundraising scenarios to the board within 45–60 days and adopt contingencies if pipeline conversion lags."

