Suggested finance narrative for the board (2–3 minutes read)
“Summit Software closed the quarter with $1.5M of cash and revenue of $1.8M for the quarter (≈$600k/month). We have reported a 20‑month runway in our materials; however, that number is inconsistent with the $45k/month burn figure in our internal summary. If the $45k figure is the net cash burn, our runway is closer to 33 months. If the runway is in fact 20 months, the true net cash burn is approximately $75k/month. We are treating this as a clarification/controls issue rather than a business emergency — the revenue profile is strong — but accuracy of cash and burn metrics is essential to board decision making (recruiting, sales investments, or fundraising). Finance will deliver a reconciled 6‑month cash flow and three forward scenarios (base growth, flat revenue, and downside with a 25% revenue shock) within 48 hours.”

