Over the last quarter Summit Software generated $1.8M in revenue (≈ $600K/month). We currently hold $1.5M in cash. Our reported net cash burn is $45K/month, which implies ~33 months of runway if current run-rate continues. The 20‑month runway figure included in earlier materials reflected planned near-term investments (hiring, product ramp, one-time platform spend) and therefore uses a higher projected monthly outflow. We are cash-flow positive on our core operations relative to the small net burn; however, to preserve optionality for growth initiatives we propose either (a) phasing planned hires to preserve >24 months runway, or (b) raising a modest round sized to fund the product roadmap through the next 12–18 months. We will deliver a reconciled cash flow statement and a 12-month scenario analysis at the board meeting.

