- 1) Revenue recognition / collection / timing risk
  - Why: High monthly revenue ($600K) but if significant bookings are deferred or customer payments slow, cash inflows can fall.
  - Impact: Rapidly shortens runway; could force emergency cost cuts or dilutive raise.
  - Mitigation: Tighten AR management, require milestone payments for large deals, monitor top 10 customers’ payment timing weekly.
  - Metric to watch: Days sales outstanding (DSO), % of revenue billed vs collected.

- 2) Customer concentration
  - Why: If a small number of customers make up >30–40% of revenue, loss or churn has outsized impact.
  - Impact: Large QoQ revenue swings; sales pipeline stress.
